ligned with the University's mission, the College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical\nSciences is committed to academic excellence, research superiority, and community\nservice. We aim to prepare our learners to take on leading roles in pharmacy, research,\nand public health. Our dedication to these principles has earned us accreditation\nthrough the Accreditation Council for Pharmacy Education (ACPE), the national agency\nresponsible for accrediting professional degree programs in pharmacy, as well as providers\nof continuing pharmacy education.\nFurthermore, the Institute of Public Health, an integral part of our academic landscape,\nis accredited through the Council on Education for Public Health (CEPH). This dual\naccreditation reflects our commitment to maintaining the highest standards in both\npharmacy education and public health initiatives.\nAs you embark on your educational journey with us, you can be confident in the quality\nof education, research opportunities, and community engagement that await you. Join\nus at the Florida A&M University College of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences,\nwhere you'll not only gain knowledge and skills but also contribute to a legacy of\nexcellence in healthcare and public health. We look forward to welcoming you to our\nvibrant learning community.\nProspective Learners\n1. Pre-Pharmacy Program Admissions\n2. PharmD Admissions\n3. Office of Student Affairs\n4. Emerging Pharmacists Summer Camp\n5. PharmD Transfer Application Criteria\n6. Explore Pharmacy\n7. Financial Aid\n8. Laptop Requirements\n9. Tuition and Fees\nApply\nVisit\nGive\nfab button\nBack to Top\n1601 S. Martin Luther King Jr Blvd, Tallahassee, FL 32307\nContact Us\n(850) 599-3000\nfacebook\ninstagram\ntwitter\nyoutube\nTerms of Use\nLegal Notice\nTitle IX\nEthics Hotline\nAccessibility\nFeedback\n\u00a9 2026 Florida Agricultural and Mechanical University.\nAll Rights Reserved\n\u00a9", "links": [["Apply", "https://admissions.famu.edu/index.php"], ["Visit", "h